rounded-full\",\"children\":\"safari names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"lion names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"lion names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"elephant names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"elephant names\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"zebra names\",{\"className\":\"text-xs bg-gray-100 text-gray-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full\",\"children\":\"zebra names\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"prose prose-lg max-w-none\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Table of Contents\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"1. The Power of African Wildlife Names | 2. Big Cat Names: Lions, Leopards, Cheetahs | 3. Elephant and Rhino Names | 4. Giraffe and Zebra Names | 5. African Language Names | 6. Safari-Inspired Names for Any Pet\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"The Power of African Wildlife Names for Pets\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"African wildlife represents the pinnacle of the natural world's majesty. The continent hosts the last great megafauna assemblages on Earth, where lions still rule the savanna, elephants shape entire landscapes, and giraffes browse treetops that no other creature can reach. African safari animal names channel this wild majesty into pet naming, giving companions names that carry the weight of the Serengeti, the mystery of the Congo basin, and the stark beauty of the Kalahari Desert. Whether your pet has lion-like confidence or zebra-like striking patterns, African wildlife provides naming inspiration of unparalleled power.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"African names also connect pets to Swahili, Zulu, Yoruba, and hundreds of other African languages. Names like Simba, which simply means lion in Swahili, carry linguistic authenticity alongside pop culture recognition from The Lion King. These language-based names demonstrate cultural awareness while providing genuinely beautiful sounds and meanings for pets. This guide explores 120+ African safari animal names across species, languages, and naming styles, helping you find a wild, wonderful name for your companion.\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Big Cat Names: Lions, Leopards, and Cheetahs\"]}],\"$La\",\"$Lb\",\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\",\"$L17\",\"$L18\",\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\"]}],\"$L20\",\"$L21\",\"$L22\",\"$L23\",\"$L24\",\"$L25\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$27\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@28\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"African big cats represent the apex of predatory evolution and provide some of the most powerful pet names available. Simba, meaning lion in Swahili, remains the most famous African animal name in the world thanks to Disney's The Lion King. Nala, Simba's queen, provides equally powerful naming for female pets. Mufasa carries kingly dignity for male companions. For actual lion-colored pets like golden retrievers and orange cats, these names create perfect visual and cultural alignment.\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Beyond The Lion King: Aslan from Narnia represents the noble lion archetype in Western literature. Leo simply means lion and works across cultures. For leopards: Chui means leopard in Swahili and carries sharp, distinctive sound. Sheba connects to the Queen of Sheba and suggests regal, mysterious beauty. For cheetahs: Duma means cheetah in Swahili and captures the speed and grace of the fastest land animal. These big cat names celebrate the power, beauty, and untamed spirit of Africa's apex predators through names that resonate across languages and cultures.\"]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Elephant and Rhinoceros Names\"]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Elephants are among the most emotionally sophisticated animals on Earth. They mourn their dead, celebrate reunions, use tools, and demonstrate empathy across species lines. Elephant names should honor their intelligence, their deep family bonds, and their gentle power. Tembo means elephant in Swahili and provides a strong, distinctive name. Jumbo, while originally a specific famous elephant, has become synonymous with large size and gentle nature. Babar, the beloved children's book elephant king, carries literary charm.\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"For smaller pets, elephant names create wonderful affectionate irony: naming a hamster Jumbo or a Chihuahua Tembo acknowledges their outsized personality in a tiny package. Rhino names channel different energy: Kifaru means rhinoceros in Swahili and carries powerful, grounded energy. Spike references the horn and armored appearance. Tank describes their massive, seemingly indestructible build. For pets with sturdy, solid personalities, rhino names capture the essence of unshakeable strength combined with surprising gentleness.\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Giraffe and Zebra Names\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Giraffes and zebras represent Africa's most visually distinctive megafauna, their unique patterns inspiring names for pets with striking appearances. Twiga means giraffe in Swahili and captures their elegant, towering beauty. Longneck describes the obvious but endearing giraffe characteristic. Tallulah combines tall reference with feminine charm. Reticulated references the beautiful net-like pattern of reticulated giraffes and works for any pet with intricate markings.\"]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Zebra names celebrate their iconic stripes: Punda means zebra in Swahili. Stripe works across species for any striped pet. Ziggy references the zigzag nature of zebra stripes. Marty, from Madagascar, connects to the most famous animated zebra. For equine pets, zebra names create clever cross-species naming: naming a horse Zeb or a pony Punda celebrates their shared equid ancestry while acknowledging their visual distinctiveness. These African herbivore names honor the grazers and browsers who shape savanna ecosystems and whose beauty rivals any predator for wild majesty.\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Beautiful African Language Names for Pets\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"African languages provide some of the most beautiful and meaningful pet names available. Swahili, spoken by approximately 200 million people across East Africa, offers especially accessible and lovely options. Zuri means beautiful. Amani means peace. Jabari means brave one. Safari simply means journey. Bahati means fortune or luck. These Swahili names carry genuine meaning while remaining phonetically accessible for English speakers.\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Beyond Swahili: Zulu names like Thandiwe (beloved) and Mandla (strength) bring Southern African linguistic beauty. Yoruba names like Ade (crown) and Ife (love) carry West African warmth. Amharic names like Desta (joy) from Ethiopia add East African linguistic diversity. These African language names celebrate the continent's extraordinary linguistic richness. Over 2,000 languages spoken across 54 countries. And give pets names that carry genuine cultural meaning rather than merely referencing wildlife. A pet named Amani or Zuri carries the beauty of Swahili language into every introduction.\"]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Safari-Inspired Names for Any Pet\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The safari experience itself provides naming inspiration beyond individual animal names. Savannah describes the iconic African landscape where most safaris occur. Sahara, the great desert, carries stark desert beauty. Kilimanjaro (or simply Kili) references Africa's tallest mountain and suits pets who rise above all challenges. Serengeti, perhaps shortened to simply Geti, describes the most famous wildlife region on Earth.\"]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Safari activity names: Trek describes the journey into wild places. Adventure captures the spirit of exploration. Explorer suits curious, boundary-testing pets. Scout works for alert, watchful companions. Sundowner references the tradition of evening drinks while watching African sunsets. Baobab, the iconic upside-down tree, provides a uniquely African botanical name. Acacia describes the umbrella-shaped trees that define safari landscapes. These safari-inspired names celebrate not just the animals of Africa but the entire experience of witnessing wildlife in its natural habitat, one of Earth's greatest remaining treasures.\"]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Birds of Africa: Ostriches, Flamingos, and Eagles\"]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"p\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"African birds provide striking and distinctive pet names often overlooked in favor of mammal megafauna. Ostrich names: Ostrich, the largest bird on Earth, contributes names celebrating height, speed, and unusual beauty. Flamingo names from Africa's soda lakes where millions of lesser flamingos gather: Moto references the Swahili word for fire, appropriate for their brilliant pink coloring. Coral and Rose capture flamingo pink without direct species reference. The secretary bird, with its distinctive crest of quills and its snake-stomping hunting technique, provides a name suggesting administrative competence with predatory edge.\"]}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"22\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"African eagle names carry soaring majesty: Tawny works for tawny eagles and golden-brown pets. Martial references Africa's largest eagle, the martial eagle, known for taking prey as large as small antelopes. Bateleur, the striking snake eagle whose name means acrobat or tightrope walker in French, describes their distinctive rocking flight. Fish Eagle, whose call is often called the voice of Africa, contributes the Swahili name Furukombe or simply Eagle. Crowned eagle, Africa's most powerful raptor capable of taking monkeys from trees. These African bird names bring avian wildness and beauty to pet naming, celebrating the feathered hunters who rule Africa's skies.\"]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"23\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"African Wild Dog and Hyena Names\"]}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"24\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Africa's wild canines provide especially fitting names for domestic dogs whose ancestry connects, however distantly, to these remarkable predators. The African wild dog, also called painted wolf or painted dog, is one of Africa's most successful hunters with pack cooperation that rivals wolves. Names drawn from their Swahili name Mbwa Mwitu or simply Painted celebrate their distinctive patchwork coats. Hyenas, while not canines, fill similar ecological niches and carry complex social intelligence. Spotted hyena clans are matriarchal, led by females who are larger and more dominant than males, inspiring female leader names like Matriarch or Queen.\"]}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"25\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/annas-hummingbird/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Anna's Hummingbird\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"53\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alligator-gar/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alligator Gar\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"70\",{\"href\":\"/animal/american-kestrel/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"American Kestrel\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"90\",{\"href\":\"/animal/andean-cock-of-the-rock/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Andean Cock-of-the-Rock\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"121\",{\"href\":\"/animal/airedale-terrier/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Airedale Terrier\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"26\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Jackal names reference Africa's smaller, more adaptable wild canines: Anubis connects to the Egyptian jackal god and carries ancient spiritual weight. Golden references the golden jackal's warm coat color. Side-striped describes the less common jackal species with distinctive flank markings. These African canid names give domestic dogs a connection to the continent where their ancestors first began the journey toward human companionship, a journey that would eventually circle the globe and produce the extraordinary diversity of breeds we know and love today. For thousands more African and wildlife-inspired names, explore bestanimalnames.com. Whether exploring the vast Serengeti plains or the dense forests of the Congo basin, African wildlife names bring the spirit of Earth's wildest continent into your home through the daily act of calling your companion by name.\"]}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"27\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Discover more naming ideas: \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"28\",{\"href\":\"/animal/goliath-birdeater/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Goliath Birdeater\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"49\",{\"href\":\"/animal/chimpanzee/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Chimpanzee\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"63\",{\"href\":\"/animal/havana-brown/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Havana Brown\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"79\",{\"href\":\"/animal/leafy-seadragon/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Leafy Seadragon\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"98\",{\"href\":\"/animal/flying-dragon/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Flying Dragon\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and hundreds more animal name generators.\"]}]\n20:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the most popular African animal names for pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Simba remains the most popular African animal pet name worldwide, followed by Nala, Mufasa, Zuri, Leo, Aslan, Sahara, and Kenya. The Lion King's cultural impact has made Swahili lion names particularly dominant, while geographical names like Sahara and Kenya offer alternative African-inspired options.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do pets respond to African language names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Pets respond to sound patterns, not language origins. African language names like Zuri, Amani, and Jabari all have clear consonant sounds and two-syllable structures that pets learn and recognize easily. The name's linguistic origin matters far less than its sound profile for training purposes.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are good African names for dogs?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"African names for dogs include Simba, Nala, Zuri (beautiful), Jabari (brave), Amani (peace), Safari (journey), Tembo (elephant), and Kibo (the highest peak of Kilimanjaro). Large breeds especially suit names referencing African megafauna like lions and elephants.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I use African names if I am not African?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"African wildlife and language names have been used globally for decades, particularly since The Lion King introduced Swahili to international audiences. Using African names demonstrates appreciation for the continent's linguistic and cultural richness. Choose names with genuine meanings and use them with respect.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What African names work well for cats specifically?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"African cat names include Simba, Nala, Mufasa, Sarabi, Chui (leopard), Duma (cheetah), and Zuri (beautiful). Cats' natural grace and predatory instincts make African big cat names especially fitting. Swahili names also tend to have the short, clear sound profiles cats recognize best.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"lion\",{\"href\":\"/animal/lion/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦁\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Lion\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"elephant\",{\"href\":\"/animal/elephant/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐘\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Elephant\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"giraffe\",{\"href\":\"/animal/giraffe/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦒\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Giraffe\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"zebra\",{\"href\":\"/animal/zebra/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦓\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Zebra\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"cheetah\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cheetah/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐆\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cheetah\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"rhinoceros\",{\"href\":\"/animal/rhinoceros/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦏\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Rhinoceros\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"grey-tree-frog\",{\"href\":\"/animal/grey-tree-frog/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐸\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Grey Tree Frog\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"kangaroo\",{\"href\":\"/animal/kangaroo/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦘\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Kangaroo\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"📖 Related Naming Guides\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"how-to-name-your-cat\",{\"href\":\"/guide/how-to-name-your-cat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How to Name Your Cat — Complete Guide 🐱\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"how-to-name-your-dog\",{\"href\":\"/guide/how-to-name-your-dog/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group flex items-center gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl\",\"children\":\"📖\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How to Name Your Dog — Complete Guide 🐕\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"afri